tag example;

exception Hold {
    value: *int
}

main() raises Hold: int {
    raise Hold { value: new int[1](1) }
}

/* expect compile {|
noregion_payload.l8:8:25

    raise Hold { value: new int[1](1) }
                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

main puts this allocation in an exception payload. An exception can
outlive the region where it was raised, leaving its payload pointing to
freed memory.

If this value should be retained, declare main as noregion. Its callers
also need noregion. This prevents those functions from being called
inside a region.

If the value is only needed temporarily, keep it local instead of
putting it in the exception payload, and use it before its region ends.

|} */
